# Example club admin is public at `/` and `/example`. Do not set these
# Convex / Better Auth keys to run or deploy the public seed club.
# No environment variables are required for `/` or `/example`.
#
# Optional algorithm tunables (same keys as the repo-root .env.example):
# TG_BT_REGULARIZATION=0.1
# TG_BT_MAX_ITERATIONS=500
# TG_BT_TOLERANCE=1e-6
# TG_MIN_COMPARISONS=3
# TG_MIN_OPPONENTS=2
# TG_TOP_K_REFERRALS=5
#
# `/club` only — official Convex + Better Auth (`@convex-dev/better-auth`).
# Not Clerk, not Neon. Unauthenticated /club shows sign-in, never the seed
# board. Signed-in owners get the Convex-backed board only when these are
# set and `npx convex dev` is running in apps/club.
#
# Sean's setup: all of these live in Doppler (project `talent-graph`, config
# `dev`). `doppler setup` (reads repo-root doppler.yaml) then run through it:
#   bun run club:web      # doppler run -- next dev
#   bun run club:convex   # doppler run -- convex dev
# No .env.local is needed. Fallback without Doppler: `npx convex dev` writes
# the NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_* keys into .env.local; add NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL.
#
# Next.js side:
# CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:adjective-animal-123
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=https://adjective-animal-123.convex.cloud
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_SITE_URL=https://adjective-animal-123.convex.site
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
#
# Convex deployment side (also mirrored in Doppler). Same SITE_URL as
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL. Already set on dev via `npx convex env set`:
# npx convex env set BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=$(openssl rand -base64 32)
# npx convex env set SITE_URL http://127.0.0.1:3000
